TINES WEBHOOK ACTION
====================

Purpose:
Receive security alert data generated by the Elastic Security
detection rule.

Source:
Elastic Security SIEM

HTTP Method:
POST

Allowed Methods:
GET, POST

Workflow Role:
The webhook acts as the entry point for the Tines workflow.
When the Elastic detection rule identifies the configured
security event, the alert information is forwarded to Tines
through the webhook.

Data Flow:

Elastic Security Detection Rule
        ↓
Webhook Connector
        ↓
Tines Webhook Action
        ↓
AI Agent

The webhook data is subsequently referenced by the AI Agent
through the webhook action data tag.

Security Note:
Webhook secrets, authentication credentials, API keys and
other sensitive values are excluded from this submission.
